WEBVTT

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.692
that would literally fit one million Earths inside it.

00:00:32.815 --> 00:00:35.000
The sun seems impossibly big,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.077
but in the great scheme of things, it's a pinprick,

00:00:39.077 --> 00:00:43.000
one of about 400 billion stars in the Milky Way galaxy,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.123
which you can see on a clear night

00:00:45.123 --> 00:00:48.123
as a pale, white mist 
stretched across the sky.

00:00:48.123 --> 00:00:49.023
And it gets worse.

00:00:49.023 --> 00:00:52.985
There are maybe 100 billion galaxies detectable by our telescopes,

00:00:53.723 --> 00:00:58.000
so if each star was the size of a single grain of sand,

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.000
just the Milky Way has enough stars to fill